# Agent Instructions — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Always follow software engineering best practices and load only the relevant skills in `.agents/skills/` for your current task. Keep this router concise; inspect [`.agents/stack-profile.md`](.agents/stack-profile.md) for active stack commands, domain evaluators, and branch conventions.

- **Engineering Philosophy (Mandatory):** Read and follow [`.agents/skills/engineering-philosophy/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/engineering-philosophy/SKILL.md) (**DRY**, **KISS**, **YAGNI**, **CAZZ**, and mandatory testing).
- **Product Strategy & Business YAGNI Gate:** Before evaluating new feature ideas, creating enhancement tickets, or running a CTO/PO architecture review, follow [`.agents/skills/product-strategy-gate/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/product-strategy-gate/SKILL.md) and [`docs/product_strategy.md`](docs/product_strategy.md).
- **Pre-Merge Quality Gate (Mandatory Before Merge):** Follow [`.agents/skills/pr-quality-gate/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/pr-quality-gate/SKILL.md): right-size review depth (`<= 3` production files vs. multi-domain parallel `research` Evaluators), run all verification commands in [`.agents/stack-profile.md`](.agents/stack-profile.md), pass an **Independent Final PR Reviewer** (`Model: 'inherit'`), verify Sandbox if applicable, and never merge with unautomated manual cloud steps.
- **Parallel & Stacked PR Orchestration (Batch / Overnight Mode):** When tackling multiple tickets in parallel or stacked PR chains, follow [`.agents/skills/parallel-pr-orchestrator/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/parallel-pr-orchestrator/SKILL.md) (`Workspace: 'share'`, `Model: 'inherit'`, strictly disjoint track files, zero unattended merges). When planning/triaging a multi-ticket backlog outside `/goal`, end your response with:
  `/goal Execute the open tickets in "<Milestone/Sprint>" using the parallel-pr-orchestrator and pr-quality-gate skills.`
- **Committed Markdown Hygiene:** Never write machine-local `file:///...` links in committed `.md` files (use portable relative paths). In Mermaid diagrams, use short single-line quoted labels without HTML tags (`<br/>`) or `\n` so text is never clipped.
